# Coding conventions

Follow `docs/coding-conventions.md`. Tooling is in `docs/repo-conventions.md`.

## Write it this way

- Pydantic models for Release, Sbom, VexDecision, ReportDraft, TechnicalFileExport, Approval. Fail at construction if invariants are missing.
- Pipeline steps are pure and idempotent. Evidence is append-only; never repair a hash.
- Evidence export and report release are gates on state changes, not dashboards. No export without a hash-bound SBOM and frozen VEX decisions. No report leaves without a named human press. VEX is superseded, never deleted.
- One package, one concern. Domain packages do not import platform SDKs.
- Names match the blueprints (`release_hash`, `product_line_id`, `vex_decision_id`). Do not invent synonyms.

```text
# ❌ BAD
if payload.get("hash"):
    export.status = "sealed"  # skip the checks
    db.commit()

# ✅ GOOD
check = ReadinessCheck.model_validate(payload)
export = lifecycle.transition(export, to="built", checks=(check,))
```
